  "body": "Requested by @vilts (relayed by the user, 2026-11-19), after the #2603 kit ran clean in his Robodrill's Manual Guide i graphic simulation: today the simulation draws a default blank, and he does not know how to set it by hand.\n\n## What\n\nManual Guide i reads a blank (stock) definition block near the top of a program and uses it in the animation. An **opt-in** Fanuc post option writes the setup's stock as that block, after the program number and before the first motion.\n\nCodes as the user's reading of the manual summarises them (to be verified against the manual):\n\n| Code | Blank |\n|---|---|\n| G1902 | rectangular block: B width (X), D depth (Y), H height (Z), I/J/K = X/Y/Z distance from the block's lowest corner to the work origin |\n| G1900 | round bar (along Z) |\n| G1906 | round bar along X |\n| G1901 / G1907 | hollow round bar (along Z / X) |\n| G1903 / G1904 | square bar / hollow square bar |\n\nExample (100 x 60 x 30 block, G54 at the top centre): `G1902 B100. D60. H30. I50. J30. K30.`\n\nSource (public Fanuc documentation, behaviour only): Manual Guide i milling and turning operator's manual, https://www.cnc.uk.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/04/Manual-Guide-Milling-and-Turning-Manual.pdf\n\n## Rules\n\n- **Off by default.** A control without Manual Guide i can alarm on G1902, so the option is per machine (a machine/post property, e.g. \"Manual Guide i blank\"), never on for every Fanuc output.\n- Box stock -> G1902; a cylinder stock -> G1900 (or G1906 when its axis is X); any other stock shape -> no block and a comment saying why, not a wrong block.\n- I/J/K come from the setup's WCS origin relative to the stock's minimum corner, in program units (G20/G21), with the signs the manual gives. A yawed or rotated WCS that the block cannot describe -> no block plus a comment.\n- No other post output changes (golden files stay the same with the option off).\n\n## Research first (agent)\n\nRead the manual's blank-figure section and confirm: the exact address letters and signs for G1902 and G1900 (incl. the bar's length and the axis position), where in the program the block must stand (before or after G90/G54, before the first tool change), whether it needs Manual Guide i \"animation\" mode only, and inch behaviour. Record the answers here before code.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The Fanuc post has the option, off by default; with it on, a box stock and a cylinder stock each post the right block (golden tests), and an unsupported stock posts a comment, not a block.\n- vilts confirms in his Manual Guide i simulation that the drawn blank matches the stock (one short kit file).\n- Clean-room: Fanuc's public manual only; no other CAM's post or output consulted.\n",
